# Rust
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local config — not committed (per repo policy on credentials)
~/.terrashift/
.env
.env.local
*.local.toml

# Reference codebases — junctions and large file copies, set up per developer
# via scripts/setup-refs.ps1. Not committed because junctions don't survive
# git and the source archives are large.
/refs/

# Test fixtures — external repos cloned for testing. Not committed because
# some are GPL-2 (incompatible with our Apache-2 distribution) and they bloat
# the repo. Set up via scripts/setup-fixtures.ps1.
/fixtures/

# Audit log working files (user data, never auto-deleted)
.audit/
.checkpoints/
.backup/

# Test artifacts
/coverage/
*.profraw

# Spec Kit feature workdirs
specs/*/output/

# Sandbox executor working directories
/tmp/terrashift-exec-*/

# Security scan artifacts (per session, not for repo)
/checkov-report.json
/checkov-stderr.txt
/package-leakage-report.json
/precommit-scan-*.md
/precommit-scan-*.html

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project governance + Claude Code workspace — TRACKED for collaboration.
#
# Reversed the previous "internal only" policy on 2026-05-04: contributors
# (human + Claude) joining the project need access to the constitution,
# the architecture plan, the seam-mapping, the Spec Kit history, and the
# `/docs/` onboarding material. None of these contain credentials —
# settings.local.json is the only Claude artefact that does, and it
# stays excluded below.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Claude Code session-local config — DOES contain user-specific paths and
# session state. Never push.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Stakpak session files — per-user runtime state.
.stakpak/session*

# Stakpak session DB + working state
.stakpak/
